Ported (Go to Rust) into crates/kgraf-orchestrator/src/reports.rs, with
significant changes stated here (Apache-2.0 section 4b):
- Constants: MaxReportTextCharacters (1000), ReportBatchFallback (1 hour),
  ReportSettlementWindow (5 minutes), ReportInterruptWindow (3 minutes).
- `Service.Create`: done reports become available after the settlement window;
  needs-input and stuck at once; other (informational) reports at the one-hour
  fallback.
- `Coordinator.deliverProject`: a stuck report interrupts at most once per
  worker per window; a batch whose only urgency is a stuck report inside the
  window is deferred ("coalesced") until the window opens, unless it also
  carries needs-input.

Changed: kGraf adds a fifth kind, contract-inadequate (decisions 0009,
0027), the only kind delivered to peers holding the contract as well as the
orchestrator. Informational reports ride along with any earlier delivery; a
done report does not. Upstream's durable outbox (claim tokens, delivery
attempts, acknowledgment, idempotency keys) is not ported: the queue lives in
the orchestrator loop, its only consumer.
